    "created_at": "2019-11-07T14:17:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-07T14:17:37Z",
    "body": "This fix isn't correct. Using this tree, where nodes are the order they should occur by stepping through nextNode():\r\n```\r\n           root\r\n            / \\\r\n           1   7\r\n          / \\\r\n         2   4\r\n        /   / \\\r\n       3   5   6\r\n\r\n```\r\nif you are at node 3 and follow the algorithm, 'temporary' points to 2, and 'sibling' points to 4. So it would return 2. The fix is is to assign node=sibling before the break.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
